// Per-round (regression):
// 1. $r \leftarrow y - F_{t-1}(x)$
// 2. $p_t \leftarrow \min(25,\, p_0(1+g\,t/T))$  with $p_0 = \mathrm{clip}(50/\sqrt{n}-0.3,\,0,5)$,\, $g = \max(0, 3 - n/1000)$
// 3. $r \leftarrow \mathrm{clip}(r,\,P_{p_t}(r),\,P_{100-p_t}(r))$
// 4. fit tree $h_t$ on $r$
// 5. $\alpha_t = \max\!\big(0,\,\frac{\langle r,h_t\rangle}{\|h_t\|^2 + \lambda}\big),\quad \lambda = \max(1,\,3-n/500)$
// 6. (small data only) $w \leftarrow \frac{1}{n}(1 + 0.2\,|y - F_t|/P_{95})$
// Classification: standard AdaBoost ($w \leftarrow w \exp(\alpha\mathbb{1}_{\hat y\ne y})$).

// Targets: $g = y-F$ (reg) or $y-\sigma(F)$ (clf)
// Learner weight (Newton with $\lambda=0.1$):
//  reg: $\alpha = \max(0, \langle g,h\rangle/(\|h\|^2+\lambda))$
//  clf: $\alpha = \max(0, \langle g,h\rangle/(\sum p(1-p)h^2+\lambda))$
// Update (regression, AdaBoost.R2):
//  $e = |h - g|/\max|h-g|$,\;$\bar e = \langle w, e\rangle$,\;$\beta = \bar e/(1-\bar e)$,\;$w \leftarrow w\,\beta^{1-e}$
// Update (classification, margin-confidence):
//  $\tau_t = 1.5 - 0.5\,t/T$;\; $s = |g|\exp(-y_{\pm}F)/\max(\cdot)$;\; $w \leftarrow w\,\exp(\tau_t\,s)$

// 1. if regression and $n<1000$: $\xi_i \sim \mathrm{Exp}(1)$ else $\xi_i = 1$
// 2. clf: $p = \sigma(F)$, $g = y-p$, $h = p(1-p)$, $\lambda=0.01$
// 3. reg: $g = y-F$, $h = 1$, $\lambda = 1.0$ if $n\le 5000$ else $0$
// 4. $w \leftarrow (h+\lambda)\,\xi + 10^{-10}$
// 5. target $= \mathrm{clip}(g/(h+\lambda),\,-20,20)$ (clf) or $\mathrm{clip}(g, -200, 200)$ (reg)
// 6. fit $h_t$ on target with sample weight $w$
// 7. $\alpha = \max(0.01,\,\langle g,h_t\rangle/(\langle h+\lambda,\,h_t^2\rangle + 10^{-10}))$
// 8. for large reg ($n>5000$): $\alpha \leftarrow 2.5\,\alpha$

// Classification:
// 1. AdaBoost $\alpha = 0.5\eta\log((1-\bar\varepsilon)/\bar\varepsilon)$
// 2. $w \leftarrow w\,e^{\alpha\mathbb{1}_{\hat y\ne y}} \cdot (0.85+0.15 e^{-|m_t|})$
// Regression (small, $n\le 5000$):
// 3. $r = y-F$;\;$s = \sqrt{\langle w,r^2\rangle}$;\;$\delta = s(1.25+1.25\,p)$
// 4. target $= r/\sqrt{1+(r/\delta)^2}$ (pseudo-Huber)
// 5. $\alpha = \mathrm{clip}\Big(\frac{\sum w r h}{\sum w h^2 + 1},\,0,\,2.5\Big)$
// 6. update $w$ as mix: $(1-f)\,U + f\,(0.15 + (z/(1+z))e^{-0.15z})$ then $w\leftarrow 0.75\,w_{\text{new}}+0.25\,w_{\text{old}}$
// Regression (large): plain residual fit, Newton step clipped to [0,4], no reweighting

// Per-round:
// 1. fit tree on $y$ (clf) or residual $r=y-F$ (reg)
// 2. clf: $\bar\varepsilon = w^\top\mathbb{1}_{\hat y\ne y}$; $\alpha = \eta\,0.5\log((1-\bar\varepsilon)/\bar\varepsilon)$
//    reg: $\alpha = \max(0, \langle r, h\rangle/(\|h\|^2+1))$
// 3. clf raw scores $S \leftarrow S + \alpha(2\hat y-1)$; margin $m = (2y-1)\tanh(S)$
// 4. clf reweight: $w \leftarrow w\cdot \mathrm{clip}(\exp(-(1+2t/T)\,m),\,0.1,\,20)$
// 5. reg: $w$ unchanged
